Now CSS jumpscare update. Note animation keyframes name. Set img fill. Maybe add slight brightness. The static overlay with screen at 0.35 over bright face adds noise but not wash. With new face mostly pale, should show. Still reduce static opacity to .2 and add mix-blend-mode: overlay? On pure black, overlay does nothing; grain over face adds texture. Use `soft-light` maybe. Keep screen at .18. Also add a red/white radial flash behind? fine.

CSS:
```
.jumpscare img {
 position:absolute; inset:0; width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover;
 transform: scale(.72);
 transform-origin: 50% 43%;
 filter: contrast(1.35) brightness(1.02) saturate(.55);
 animation: scareLunge .62s cubic-bezier(...) forwards;
}
@keyframes scareLunge {
 0% { transform: scale(.62); opacity:.15; filter: contrast(1.1) brightness(.7) saturate(.4) blur(3px);}
 30% { transform: scale(1.04); opacity:1; filter: contrast(1.45) brightness(1.08) saturate(.5) blur(0);}
 100% { transform: scale(1.16); opacity:1;}
}
```
Careful filter animation maybe costly but only 1.2s. Fine.

Static opacity .22; add `background-size: 160px`.

Also add `will-change: transform`.

